    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the acceptance suite is the only test class with test methods). Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional `postcode` (4-digit) field to owners, validated **only when present** against a fixed region table, stored and returned end-to-end.\n\n**Contract / DTO** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: added an optional `postcode` string property (`pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`, not in `required`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf OwnerFields`, this flows into both the request and response DTOs; MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 `Owner.java`: new `postcode` column + getter/setter. Added the `postcode` column to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files (hsqldb is what the test profile uses with `ddl-auto=none`, so this was required; the others kept consistent).\n\n**Validation (the 400 path)** \u2014 the create pipeline binds the body *without* `@Valid`, so schema patterns aren't auto-enforced there. Following the existing `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`/`InvalidTelephoneException` pattern:\n- `ValidateOwnerPostcode` \u2014 no-op when postcode absent/blank; else requires 4 digits and, via `PostcodeRegions`, that it falls in the city's region range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099). Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode. Throws the checked `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n- `PostcodeRegions` \u2014 region\u2192range table; derives the region by reusing the existing `LocalityLookup.regionOf(city)`.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2192 400 with `{\"error\": ...}`.\n- Wired `validatePostcode` into `owners.POST.yml` (after email normalization, before identity checks).\n\n**Update path (for spec completeness)** \u2014 added the same `validatePostcode` step to `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` and `owner.setPostcode(...)` to `ApplyOwner`.\n\n**Test results:** `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 3/3 pass (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`); full `./mvnw test` is green.\n\nOne note on a design choice worth surfacing: I set the DB column width to `VARCHAR(4)` to match the 4-digit contract. If you'd rather keep the column permissive against future format changes, say the word and I'll widen it.",
